# --skip-to-area rows for Spyro 3 (fields: flag | target | engagement | frame_limit | bk2).
# A row runs headless with `<flag> <target>` and passes only when stderr
# carries the engagement text before frame_limit VBLs; the fail-safe line or
# no engagement line fails it. bk2 is a movie replayed with
# --bk2-frame-offset 0 for a row whose route needs pad input, or `-`.
# Every sub-area 1..N-1 of the 17 multi-area levels is entered by one area-0
# portal.
--skip-to-area | 11:1 | [skip-to-area] released: level=11 area=1 | 6000 | -
--skip-to-area | 11:2 | [skip-to-area] released: level=11 area=2 | 6000 | -
--skip-to-area | 12:1 | [skip-to-area] released: level=12 area=1 | 6000 | -
